{"toolCallId":"call_6c565144e32d4505aa1445a569f46858","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `T` is a temp fixture folder whose report prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the option loop, the tail and the exit-code comment in `S`, and record the current exit codes. Verify: `rg -n 'exit [0-9]' \"$S\"` prints the existing `exit 0` plus the error exits.\n- [ ] T002 Build the fixture: `T=$(mktemp -d); printf '[TBD]\\n' > \"$T/spec.md\"`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$T\"` prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Capture the baseline report for later diffing: `bash \"$S\" \"$T\" > baseline.txt`. Verify: the command exits 0 and `wc -l < baseline.txt` prints a non-zero count.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add a `MIN_PERCENT` global and a `--min-percent` case to the option loop that validates `^[0-9]+$` and a value from 0 to 100, exiting 1 with a stderr usage error otherwise (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent abc \"$T\"` exits 1 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\"` is accepted.\n- [ ] T005 Replace the unconditional `exit 0` with the threshold comparison, using `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the single-file percentage under `--file`, so a completion below `MIN_PERCENT` exits 3 and anything else exits 0 (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\"` exits 3 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$T\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--min-percent <N>` line to `show_help` and list exit 3 in the trailing exit-code comment (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` prints one `--min-percent` line and `rg -n '3 - ' \"$S\"` prints the below-threshold entry.\n- [ ] T007 [P] Confirm the option appears only where intended (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'min-percent|MIN_PERCENT' \"$S\"` lists hits only in `show_help`, the option loop and the tail, with none inside `output_text` or `output_json`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T008 Run the exit matrix on the fixture. Verify: no option exits 0, `--min-percent 0` exits 0, `--min-percent 1` exits 3 and `--min-percent 90` exits 3.\n- [ ] T009 Diff the text report with and without the option. Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" \"$T\" || true) <(bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\" || true)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T010 [P] Diff the JSON report with and without the option. Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" --json \"$T\" || true) <(bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 90 \"$T\" || true)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T011 Run the matrix on a fully complete packet folder. Verify: `--min-percent 100` on `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent` exits 0, and `--min-percent 101` exits 1 with a stderr message.\n- [ ] T012 Run spec validation on this packet as a regression check. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] Exit matrix and both output diffs recorded in `implementation-summary.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `T` is a temp fixture folder whose report prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the option loop, the tail and the exit-code comment in `S`, and record the current exit codes. Verify: `rg -n 'exit [0-9]' \"$S\"` prints the existing `exit 0` plus the error exits.\n- [ ] T002 Build the fixture: `T=$(mktemp -d); printf '[TBD]\\n' > \"$T/spec.md\"`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$T\"` prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Capture the baseline report for later diffing: `bash \"$S\" \"$T\" > baseline.txt`. Verify: the command exits 0 and `wc -l < baseline.txt` prints a non-zero count.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add a `MIN_PERCENT` global and a `--min-percent` case to the option loop that validates `^[0-9]+$` and a value from 0 to 100, exiting 1 with a stderr usage error otherwise (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent abc \"$T\"` exits 1 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\"` is accepted.\n- [ ] T005 Replace the unconditional `exit 0` with the threshold comparison, using `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the single-file percentage under `--file`, so a completion below `MIN_PERCENT` exits 3 and anything else exits 0 (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\"` exits 3 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$T\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--min-percent <N>` line to `show_help` and list exit 3 in the trailing exit-code comment (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` prints one `--min-percent` line and `rg -n '3 - ' \"$S\"` prints the below-threshold entry.\n- [ ] T007 [P] Confirm the option appears only where intended (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'min-percent|MIN_PERCENT' \"$S\"` lists hits only in `show_help`, the option loop and the tail, with none inside `output_text` or `output_json`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T008 Run the exit matrix on the fixture. Verify: no option exits 0, `--min-percent 0` exits 0, `--min-percent 1` exits 3 and `--min-percent 90` exits 3.\n- [ ] T009 Diff the text report with and without the option. Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" \"$T\" || true) <(bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\" || true)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T010 [P] Diff the JSON report with and without the option. Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" --json \"$T\" || true) <(bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 90 \"$T\" || true)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T011 Run the matrix on a complete fixture: `C=$(mktemp -d); printf '## 1. METADATA\\nFilled content.\\n' > \"$C/spec.md\"`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 100 \"$C\"` exits 0 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 101 \"$C\"` exits 1 with a stderr message.\n- [ ] T012 Run spec validation on this packet as a regression check. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] Exit matrix and both output diffs recorded in `implementation-summary.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_6f334a1b16af477cb6119765c565cdcf","title":"Ran bash, rg","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent 2>&1 | rg \"Overall Completion|Total Placeholders|Files Analyzed\"","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent 2>&1 | rg \"Overall Completion|Total Placeholders|Files Analyzed\"","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["bash","rg"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_80b5c60a17484f579703662e1a9f379e","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one validated option and one conditional exit to calculate-completeness.sh. The report functions stay untouched; the tail compares the percentage it already computed with N and exits 3 on a shortfall.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell script |\n| **Framework** | None - system-spec-kit CLI |\n| **Storage** | None - reads spec Markdown files |\n| **Testing** | Bash exit-status matrix plus `diff` of stdout on a temp fixture |\n\n### Overview\nChange one file, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. The argument loop gains a validated `--min-percent <N>` case and the unconditional `exit 0` at the end becomes a comparison against the percentage the script already computed. The report functions are not edited, so stdout stays byte-identical; a temp folder with a known completion proves both the exit matrix and the unchanged output.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Exit matrix verified: below N exits 3, at or above N exits 0, no option exits 0\n- [ ] Report output diffed clean with and without the option in text and JSON modes\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script option branch.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument loop (section 8, MAIN SCRIPT)**: parses `--min-percent <N>`, validates it as an integer from 0 to 100, and stores it in a `MIN_PERCENT` global that defaults to empty.\n- **Completion calculation (section 6)**: unchanged; produces `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the file `percentage` under `--file`.\n- **Output functions (section 7)**: unchanged; print the report before any threshold decision runs.\n- **Exit decision (section 8, after the output call)**: reads the same percentage the report printed, compares it with `MIN_PERCENT`, and exits 3 or 0.\n\n### Data Flow\nargv enters the option loop, which sets `MIN_PERCENT` and leaves the folder or `--file` path in place. `calculate_spec_completeness` or `calculate_file_completeness` fills the percentage, `output_text` or `output_json` prints the report, and the tail compares that percentage with `MIN_PERCENT`. When `MIN_PERCENT` is empty the tail keeps the current `exit 0`; when it is set and the completion is lower, the script exits 3.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nUse a temp fixture with a known completion: `tmp=$(mktemp -d); printf '[TBD]\\n' > \"$tmp/spec.md\"` gives one placeholder over one content line, so the report prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n\n| Check | Command | Expected |\n|-------|---------|----------|\n| Below threshold | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 \"$tmp\"` | exit 3 |\n| At threshold | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 0 \"$tmp\"` | exit 0 |\n| No option | `calculate-completeness.sh \"$tmp\"` | exit 0 |\n| Text output unchanged | `diff <(calculate-completeness.sh \"$tmp\" \\|\\| true) <(calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 \"$tmp\" \\|\\| true)` | no output |\n| JSON output unchanged | same diff with `--json` on both sides | no output |\n| Bad value | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 101 \"$tmp\"` | exit 1, stderr message, empty stdout |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n`bash` 3.2 or newer and `bc`, which the script already requires and guards. No new package and no change to the existing `bc` check.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\nTrigger: the invocation without `--min-percent` changes its output or its exit status. Revert the one scoped commit to `calculate-completeness.sh`; the option is additive and writes no state, so nothing else needs cleanup.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one validated option and one conditional exit to calculate-completeness.sh. The report functions stay untouched; the tail compares the percentage it already computed with N and exits 3 on a shortfall.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell script |\n| **Framework** | None - system-spec-kit CLI |\n| **Storage** 