{"toolCallId":"call_e76811fa08a848ebbdb61cd9e7a20108","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\nN/A — record any testing beyond the verification tasks in `tasks.md` here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\nN/A — record dependencies beyond the components named in the architecture here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\nN/A — record rollback steps beyond reverting the scoped change here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one validated option and one conditional exit to calculate-completeness.sh. The report functions stay untouched; the tail compares the percentage it already computed with N and exits 3 on a shortfall.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell script |\n| **Framework** | None - system-spec-kit CLI |\n| **Storage** | None - reads spec Markdown files |\n| **Testing** | Bash exit-status matrix plus `diff` of stdout on a temp fixture |\n\n### Overview\nChange one file, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. The argument loop gains a validated `--min-percent <N>` case and the unconditional `exit 0` at the end becomes a comparison against the percentage the script already computed. The report functions are not edited, so stdout stays byte-identical; a temp folder with a known completion proves both the exit matrix and the unchanged output.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Exit matrix verified: below N exits 3, at or above N exits 0, no option exits 0\n- [ ] Report output diffed clean with and without the option in text and JSON modes\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script option branch.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument loop (section 8, MAIN SCRIPT)**: parses `--min-percent <N>`, validates it as an integer from 0 to 100, and stores it in a `MIN_PERCENT` global that defaults to empty.\n- **Completion calculation (section 6)**: unchanged; produces `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the file `percentage` under `--file`.\n- **Output functions (section 7)**: unchanged; print the report before any threshold decision runs.\n- **Exit decision (section 8, after the output call)**: reads the same percentage the report printed, compares it with `MIN_PERCENT`, and exits 3 or 0.\n\n### Data Flow\nargv enters the option loop, which sets `MIN_PERCENT` and leaves the folder or `--file` path in place. `calculate_spec_completeness` or `calculate_file_completeness` fills the percentage, `output_text` or `output_json` prints the report, and the tail compares that percentage with `MIN_PERCENT`. When `MIN_PERCENT` is empty the tail keeps the current `exit 0`; when it is set and the completion is lower, the script exits 3.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nUse a temp fixture with a known completion: `tmp=$(mktemp -d); printf '[TBD]\\n' > \"$tmp/spec.md\"` gives one placeholder over one content line, so the report prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n\n| Check | Command | Expected |\n|-------|---------|----------|\n| Below threshold | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 \"$tmp\"` | exit 3 |\n| At threshold | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 0 \"$tmp\"` | exit 0 |\n| No option | `calculate-completeness.sh \"$tmp\"` | exit 0 |\n| Text output unchanged | `diff <(calculate-completeness.sh \"$tmp\" \\|\\| true) <(calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 \"$tmp\" \\|\\| true)` | no output |\n| JSON output unchanged | same diff with `--json` on both sides | no output |\n| Bad value | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 101 \"$tmp\"` | exit 1, stderr message, empty stdout |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n`bash` 3.2 or newer and `bc`, which the script already requires and guards. No new package and no change to the existing `bc` check.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\nTrigger: the invocation without `--min-percent` changes its output or its exit status. Revert the one scoped commit to `calculate-completeness.sh`; the option is additive and writes no state, so nothing else needs cleanup.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":26,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":23}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
